       "attachment_id": "pub_toolu_bdrk_01MUFLAqqYPo7PvqX3j9xUGM_output"
      }
     },
     "text": "",
     "type": "output_text"
    },
    {
     "annotations": [],
     "text": "### Key Findings\n\n**Lowest cancellation rates:**\n- **Sardinia** (20.6%)\n- **Dubai** (20.7%)\n- **Krabi** (21.0%)\n- **Singapore** (21.1%)\n\n**Highest cancellation rates:**\n- **London** (25.1%)\n- **Munich** (24.1%)\n- **Osaka** (23.1%)\n- **Rome** (23.0%)\n\nThe top three destinations by booking volume (Phuket, Gold Coast, Mallorca) all maintain relatively moderate cancellation rates between **21.1% and 21.5%**, suggesting their popularity is not significantly impacted by cancellations. European cities tend to have slightly higher cancellation rates compared to Asian beach destinations.\n\n*Period: 2025 bookings (data through July 30, 2025)*",
     "type": "output_text"
    }
   ],
